User-specified dimensions. Build an R × C matrix of zeros and fill it. The one trap is Python''s [[0] * C] * R, which repeats the same row object R times:
rows, cols = 3, 4
bad = [[0] * cols] * rows          # three references to ONE row
bad[0][0] = 1
for r in bad:
    print(*r)                      # the 1 shows up in every row

good = [[0] * cols for _ in range(rows)]   # a fresh row each time
good[0][0] = 1
for r in good:
    print(*r)
